88c102eb646719e0.prompt:
Write one complete phone screen as JSON: {id,title?,components:[{id,c,...props}]}. Use unique snake_case ids for components; never put ids on array items. Use only listed props. Use null for absent optional fields, never write empty strings.

Layout: house/home_scenes. Job: The house's devices and scenes.

Recipe slots: [{"id":"slot_0","allow":["Header"],"min":1,"max":1},{"id":"slot_1","allow":["Devices"],"min":1,"max":1,"variant":"tiles"},{"id":"slot_2","allow":["Note"],"min":1,"max":1}]. Match every required slot in order. Variants such as shelf, reply, month or mood are the component's style; Field/Camera variants are kind. prices means every Choice option has a price value; toggle means every List row has trail: toggle.

Screen rules: three to nine components outside overlays, total weight at most twelve, at most two weight-three components. One primary Button at most. Hero first in the body; a SectionTitle needs following content. Repeated types cannot be adjacent except Card and Field. Reply Composer is last after Bubbles. Do not invent color, size or layout props.

Layout rule: Keep saved scenes on Devices in tiles style, above the rooms. With an empty cast an empty scenes seed is valid; do not invent device references or claim commands succeeded.

Real app content: {"things":[],"items":[]}

Header: Name the screen and offer one optional shortcut.
props: { style?: large|inline|back="large", title: text≤28, sub?: text≤40, action?: { icon: dot|leaf|drop|dog|cat|calendar|calendar_days|clock|check|chevron_right|plus|minus|close|search|settings|bell|bell_off|heart|star|bookmark|share|send|message|mail|phone|camera|image|video|mic|music|play|pause|square|undo|timer|alarm_clock|sun|moon|cloud|cloud_rain|thermometer|wind|flame|zap|battery|wifi|pin|map|navigation|compass|home|building|store|shopping_cart|shopping_bag|tag|gift|credit_card|wallet|banknote|piggy_bank|receipt|trending_up|trending_down|bar_chart|pie_chart|activity|target|trophy|medal|award|flag|user|users|user_plus|baby|smile|dumbbell|bike|footprints|heart_pulse|pill|stethoscope|apple|coffee|utensils|wine|pizza|carrot|sprout|flower|tree|mountain|waves|car|bus|plane|train|briefcase|graduation_cap|book_open|book|pencil|file_text|clipboard|clipboard_list|checklist|lock|unlock|key|shield|eye|link|paperclip|download|upload|trash|edit|filter|sliders|info|alert|help|sparkles|lightbulb|palette|scissors|wrench|hammer|package|truck|recycle|globe|languages|gamepad|ticket|paw|shirt|bed|bath|sofa|lamp|chevron_left|arrow_left|more|external_link|quote|circle_check, label: text≤16, goto?: id snake_case } }
example: {"c":"Header","style":"large","title":"My plants","sub":"Three need water today","action":{"icon":"plus","label":"Add a plant","goto":"new_plant"}}
weight: 1

Devices: Read and control connected household devices and apply saved settings together.
props: { rooms: [1..4 { label: text≤16, devices: [1..6 { key: text≤24, name: text≤16, kind: light|heat|plug|lock|fan|blind|sensor, on?: boolean, level?: num 0..100, temp?: num 5..30, reading?: number, unit?: celsius|percent|ppm|lux, normal?: { low: number, high: number }, goto?: id snake_case }] }], scenes?: [0..6 { name: text≤24, targets: [2..6 { key: text≤24, on?: boolean, level?: num 0..100, temp?: num 5..30 }] }]=[], focus?: text≤24, style?: tiles|focused="tiles" }
Rule: Use unique keys across all rooms. Light/heat/plug/lock/fan require on; lock on:true means locked. Heat requires temp 5–30 °C and may have reading; heat MUST have level:null, unit:null, normal:null. Celsius is implicit for heat: never write unit:celsius on a thermostat.
Rule: Sensors require reading and unit (celsius, percent, ppm, lux), optionally normal:{low,high} with low<=high. Sensors MUST have on:null, level:null, temp:null. Light/fan/blind may have level 0–100; blinds MUST have on:null. All non-heat devices MUST have temp:null. Only sensors have unit/normal, only heat/sensor have reading; use null for unsupported optional fields.
Rule: Scenes default to []. Each has 2–6 distinct device targets, with key and at least one supported absolute on/level/temp setting. Never target sensors or unknown keys. focus must name a device.
Rule: Never write active-scene, out-of-range, pending or command-outcome flags. Code chooses apply versus secure from lock targets. Lock changes and lock scenes always confirm.
Rule: Valid heat: {"key":"heat","name":"Thermostat","kind":"heat","on":true,"level":null,"temp":21,"reading":20.5,"unit":null,"normal":null,"goto":null}. Valid blind scene target: {"key":"blind","on":null,"level":0,"temp":null}. Scene targets obey the referenced device kind, not the other devices in the scene.
example: {"c":"Devices","rooms":[{"label":"Living room","devices":[{"key":"heat","name":"Thermostat","kind":"heat","on":true,"temp":21,"reading":20.5,"goto":"heating"},{"key":"humidity","name":"Humidity","kind":"sensor","reading":45,"unit":"percent","normal":{"low":40,"high":60}},{"key":"lamp","name":"Plant lamp","kind":"light","on":true,"level":70}]}],"focus":"heat","style":"focused","scenes":[{"name":"Evening","targets":[{"key":"lamp","on":true,"level":40},{"key":"heat","temp":20}]}]}
