Write one complete phone screen as JSON: {id,title?,components:[{id,c,...props}]}. Use unique snake_case ids for components; never put ids on array items. Use only listed props. Use null for absent optional fields, never write empty strings.

Layout: house/home_control. Job: The house's devices and scenes.

Recipe slots: [{"id":"slot_0","allow":["Header"],"min":1,"max":1,"variant":"back"},{"id":"slot_1","allow":["Devices"],"min":1,"max":1,"variant":"focused"},{"id":"slot_2","allow":["Note"],"min":1,"max":1}]. Match every required slot in order. Variants such as shelf, reply, month or mood are the component's style; Field/Camera variants are kind. prices means every Choice option has a price value; toggle means every List row has trail: toggle.

Screen rules: three to nine components outside overlays, total weight at most twelve, at most two weight-three components. One primary Button at most. Hero first in the body; a SectionTitle needs following content. Repeated types cannot be adjacent except Card and Field. Reply Composer is last after Bubbles. Do not invent color, size or layout props.

Layout rule: Use focused style with focus naming an existing device key, or omit focus to use the first device. No standalone slider preference replaces the connected device. Every scene target follows its referenced device's capabilities: blind targets have on:null and temp:null, only level; heat targets have level:null; sensors cannot be targets.

