ee9177abaaa5f943.prompt:
Write one complete phone screen as JSON: {id,title?,components:[{id,c,...props}]}. Use unique snake_case ids for components; never put ids on array items. Use only listed props. Use null for absent optional fields, never write empty strings.

Layout: family/board. Job: The household this week.

Brief: The household's people, shared chores and whose turn it is
Return compact JSON. When a layout says to omit a field the schema requires, write null for it instead.

Recipe slots: [{"id":"slot_0","allow":["Header"],"min":1,"max":1},{"id":"slot_1","allow":["People"],"min":1,"max":1,"variant":"stack"},{"id":"slot_2","allow":["Chores"],"min":1,"max":1},{"id":"slot_3","allow":["Turns"],"min":1,"max":1}]. Match every required slot in order. Variants such as shelf, reply, month or mood are the component's style; Field/Camera variants are kind. prices means every Choice option has a price value; toggle means every List row has trail: toggle.

Screen rules: three to nine components outside overlays, total weight at most twelve, at most two weight-three components. One primary Button at most. Hero first in the body; a SectionTitle needs following content. Repeated types cannot be adjacent except Card and Field. Reply Composer is last after Bubbles. Do not invent color, size or layout props.

Real app content: {"things":[],"items":[]}

Header: Name the screen and offer one optional shortcut.
props: { style?: large|inline|back="large", title: text≤28, sub?: text≤40, action?: { icon: dot|leaf|drop|dog|cat|calendar|calendar_days|clock|check|chevron_right|plus|minus|close|search|settings|bell|bell_off|heart|star|bookmark|share|send|message|mail|phone|camera|image|video|mic|music|play|pause|square|undo|timer|alarm_clock|sun|moon|cloud|cloud_rain|thermometer|wind|flame|zap|battery|wifi|pin|map|navigation|compass|home|building|store|shopping_cart|shopping_bag|tag|gift|credit_card|wallet|banknote|piggy_bank|receipt|trending_up|trending_down|bar_chart|pie_chart|activity|target|trophy|medal|award|flag|user|users|user_plus|baby|smile|dumbbell|bike|footprints|heart_pulse|pill|stethoscope|apple|coffee|utensils|wine|pizza|carrot|sprout|flower|tree|mountain|waves|car|bus|plane|train|briefcase|graduation_cap|book_open|book|pencil|file_text|clipboard|clipboard_list|checklist|lock|unlock|key|shield|eye|link|paperclip|download|upload|trash|edit|filter|sliders|info|alert|help|sparkles|lightbulb|palette|scissors|wrench|hammer|package|truck|recycle|globe|languages|gamepad|ticket|paw|shirt|bed|bath|sofa|lamp|chevron_left|arrow_left|more|external_link|quote|circle_check, label: text≤16, goto?: id snake_case } }
example: {"c":"Header","style":"large","title":"My plants","sub":"Three need water today","action":{"icon":"plus","label":"Add a plant","goto":"new_plant"}}
weight: 1

People: Who else is involved, with their names and roles.
props: { style?: rows|stack="rows", more?: int 1..999, members: [1..6 { name: text≤24, role?: text≤24, photo?: photo lib:<tag>|local:<n>, goto?: id snake_case }] }
example: {"c":"People","members":[{"name":"Maya","role":"Waters on weekends"}]}
weight: 2

Chores: Share recurring household jobs with owners and points earned for completing them.
props: { chores: [1..6 { title: text≤28, who: text≤16, photo?: photo lib:<tag>|local:<n>, repeat: never|daily|weekdays|weekly|monthly|yearly, every: int 1..12, last?: date YYYY-MM-DD, points?: num 0..100, goto: id snake_case }] }
Rule: Write last completion, repeat and every, never next due, overdue or done-for-now. Completion awards points and advances the due date in code.
example: {"c":"Chores","chores":[{"title":"Mist the fern","who":"Sam","photo":"lib:people","repeat":"daily","every":1,"last":"2026-11-16","points":5,"goto":"fern"},{"title":"Dust shelves","who":"Alex","repeat":"weekly","every":1,"points":10,"goto":"shelves"}]}
weight: 2

Turns: Rotate one household duty through people and advance or skip the current turn.
props: { job: text≤24, people: [2..6 { name: text≤16, photo?: photo lib:<tag>|local:<n> }], at: int 0..5 }
Rule: at is a zero-based index smaller than people.length. The next people and next index are computed.
example: {"c":"Turns","job":"Mist the plants","people":[{"name":"Sam"},{"name":"Alex"},{"name":"Mia"}],"at":0}
weight: 2

A valid default for this layout: {"id":"family_board","components":[{"id":"h1","c":"Header","style":"large","title":"Item one"},{"id":"p1","c":"People","members":[{"name":"Item one"},{"name":"Item two"},{"name":"Item three"}],"style":"stack"},{"id":"c1","c":"Chores","chores":[{"title":"Item one","who":"Item one","repeat":"weekly","every":1,"goto":"detail"}]},{"id":"t1","c":"Turns","job":"Item one","people":[{"name":"Item one"},{"name":"Item two"}],"at":0}]}

Use the supplied facts, not content from examples. Do not invent dates, status, measurements, or zero values for missing data. Keep all components focused on the screen's job; give the main action a clear label and avoid duplicate or unrelated actions. Reply with JSON only.

